Defects found:

- **Idempotency guard satisfied by its own marker:** line 50. Exact input: any target file containing:
```html
/* Auto-generate manuscript Methods & Results text (no manual click needed) */
                // Auto-regenerate report if it was previously generated
                const reportEl = document.getElementById('report-content');
                if (reportEl && !reportEl.classList.contains('hidden')) ReportEngine.generate();
```
Consequence: the file is reported `SKIP ... already-migrated` even though neither injected call exists.

- **Status code reporting the wrapper rather than the work:** lines 73-77. Exact input: all three files in `LEGACY_APPS` contain the marker-only input above, then run `python scripts/fix_legacy_auto_manuscript.py --apply`. Consequence: all three are counted as skips, `fail == 0`, and the process exits 0 without applying the migration.

- **Line endings changed outside the intended edit:** lines 52 and 58. Exact input bytes for any target file:
```python
b"alpha\n                // Auto-regenerate report if it was previously generated\r\n                const reportEl = document.getElementById('report-content');\r\n                if (reportEl && !reportEl.classList.contains('hidden')) ReportEngine.generate();\r\nomega\n"
```
Consequence: `--apply` rewrites the unrelated LF-only `alpha`/`omega` lines to CRLF, creating false content churn.

